# engram — working rules

Applies to the whole repo. The `.ai/` contract below is machine-owned.

## Commands (verify before proposing a patch)

```bash
npm run typecheck && npm test
node build/src/cli.js dump --json
node build/src/cli.js sync
node --test build/test/fingerprint.test.js    # single suite
```

## Boundaries

- `src/core/` is the leaf: no imports from `commands/`, `adapters/`, `templates/meta-prompt.ts`.
- `src/templates/` never touches the filesystem; it returns strings.
- `src/adapters/` never touches the filesystem; content is passed in by `src/commands/`.
- Generated skill carriers (`.cursor/skills/`, `.claude/`, `.pi/`, `.gemini/`, `.github/prompts/`)
  are edited through `.ai/skills/<name>.md` plus `engram sync`.

## Hard rules

- Zero runtime dependencies; `package.json` has no `dependencies` field.
- ESM, `NodeNext`: relative imports end in `.js`, type-only imports use `import type`.
- Never hand-edit the block between `<!-- engram:contract:start -->` and `<!-- engram:contract:end -->`.
- New public behaviour needs a test in `test/`.
- `tsconfig.json` `outDir` and `package.json` `bin` must name the same directory.

## Done means

`npm test` green · `npm run typecheck` clean · `engram dump` within budget · new decisions,
pitfalls and task state written into `.ai/` in the same change.

